We'll be releasing version 0.6-6 in the next couple of days, we hope.

That will include two experimental features: nimbleExternalCall, for calling external compiled code from a model or nimbleFunction; and nimbleRcall, for calling an R function from a compiled model or nimbleFunction.  I think the latter will do what you need.  You might need to write an R function to wrap the call the nearPD if any of the arguments or return value are expected to be not simply numeric objects.  They are marked "experimental" because they are new and not as general as could be, but they should work fine.

If you want to try them right away, they are on github branch "devel"

Having said all that, I skimmed the source code you linked to and it does look like all of it could be translated to a compilable nimbleFunction.  If you want to continue with that idea, you could send me off-list the translation you started and one of us could try to help.

Perry

